bin
# `make build` writes to build/, but a stray root-level uptickd (from `go build
# ./cmd/uptickd`, a manual build or a copied CI artifact) shows up as untracked
# and is 200 MB - one `git add -A` would put a binary blob into the repository
# and every future clone. Anchored to the root so build/uptickd is unaffected.
/uptickd
tools/bin/*
docs/_build
docs/tutorial
docs/node_modules
docs/modules
dist
tools-stamp
docs-tools-stamp
proto-tools-stamp
golangci-lint
keyring_test_cosmos
./**/node_modules
./**/dist
secret.yml
artifacts/*
github.com/
